{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And it became a serpent.</b> Why did He show him, may He be exalted, a serpent rather than any other thing? Because just as the serpent bites and kills, so Pharaoh and his servants bite and kill Israel. And the fact that [the serpent] turned back into a staff hinted that Pharaoh and his servants would become dry as wood. And [his] hand, which was leprous — so too Pharaoh and his servants are impure and render Israel impure; and behold, it returned like his flesh — a hint that Israel would be purified from the impurity of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:37.639409398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}